About the URDF and Mesh Files

 The UR3 robot model used in this project comes from the official MathWorks support package. The URDF and mesh files are not included in this GitHub repository because:

 1. They are part of the MATLAB support package installed locally on your machine.

 2. They are large and not required to run the Simulink model (ur3_model.slx) – the Simulink model already contains the robot’s structure.

 3. Including them would unnecessarily bloat the repository and may raise licensing concerns.

How to obtain the URDF files (if needed)

If you need to regenerate the Simulink model from scratch or work with the URDF directly:

 1. In MATLAB, go to Home tab → Add-Ons → Get Hardware Support Packages.

 2. Search for "Universal Robots UR Series Manipulators" and install it.

 3. After installation, the URDF files will be located in a folder similar to:

/Users/<your-username>/Documents/MATLAB/SupportPackages/R2025b/toolbox/robotics/supportpackages/robotlibrary/Robots/ur_description/urdf/
The UR3 file is named universalUR3.urdf.

Follow the steps in the documentation to import the robot into MATLAB and regenerate the Simulink model.

